.TH ASENSE 1 "2 August 2026" "ASense 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asense \- Acer laptop control center
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B asense
.RI [ option ]
.br
.B asense
.B probe
.RI [ --summary ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ASense
is a graphical Linux control center for supported Acer Predator and Nitro
laptops.  Available controls are discovered independently from Linux
platform-profile, hwmon, Acer WMI and supported HID interfaces.
.PP
Running the command without an option opens or focuses the graphical control
panel.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B probe, --probe
Print the authoritative local, read-only schema-3 JSON capability report to
standard output.  Redirect it with
.BR "asense probe > asense-probe.json" .
The probe performs no upload or default mutation.
.TP
.B probe --summary, --probe --summary
Print a bounded human-readable view of a fresh schema-3 capture.  This is for
quick inspection and does not replace the JSON attachment in a support report.
.TP
.B --toggle
Open ASense when it is closed, or close the existing ASense window.
.SH PROBE PRIVACY
The default probe excludes serials, UUIDs, hostname, user, network, boot and
storage identity, HID serials and physical paths, journals, raw ACPI tables,
absolute device paths and the process environment.  It reports bounded model,
kernel, power, driver and known WMI/HID transport evidence.  Review the JSON
before sharing it.  Capture observed behavior and the report with the same
ASense build, boot and loaded-module state.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/asense/desktop-user
Desktop account authorized to use the private ASense control socket.
.TP
.I /run/asense-control.sock
Private socket used to communicate with the privileged ASense daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asense-configure-user (8)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/fladirm/asense/issues.
